  "summary": "DIR-067 COMPLETE. (1) RECRUITER DOWNLOAD REPAIR: EmployerApplicantPipeline.jsx no longer builds a dead-end .html blob (the Blob + URL.createObjectURL + a[download]='-resume.html' path is deleted). The drawer now has distinct PDF and Word (DOCX) buttons that call downloadResumePdf / downloadResumeDocx from src/utils/exportDownloader.js with endpoint /api/public-export and /api/public-export-docx, withAuth false, per-button loading labels, an aria-label each, and a role=alert error banner. KEY GAP FOUND AND CLOSED: the only DOCX route was OWNER-scoped (/api/export-docx via req.user.uid), so a recruiter could never export a candidate's Word file. I added POST /api/public-export-docx to backend/index.js that mirrors the public PDF authorization EXACTLY - repo.getPublicResume, isPublished===true, publicationMode==='explicit', the owner isMembershipActive entitlement gate - reusing resolveExportTemplate + createResumeDocx, validating resumeId and EXPORTABLE_TEMPLATE, trusting NO owner session (no req.user.uid), and sitting behind exportAccountLimiter plus the public-path CSRF allowlist, so it is published-only and IDOR-safe. (2) ADAPTIVE PARTITIONER ORPHAN PREVENTION: extracted the greedy packer into a reusable packSections(sectionGapPx). (A) Adaptive Micro-Compaction re-packs with an 11px section rhythm whenever the two-page result has a minor trailing overflow (<=60px or a single trailing row) and adopts it ONLY when the whole resume then fits one page; the chosen rhythm is returned as sectionGapPx and SmartResumeComposer.jsx pins it as an inline --smart-section-gap so the painted gap always equals the estimate (no footer overlap). (B) Section Integrity & Orphan Guard moves a whole continuation section onto the last page when that page would otherwise hold a single isolated card/row of a section that continues from an earlier page, reverting if the receiving page would overflow. FUNCTIONAL PROOF: a 2 x 7 x 9 x 11 profile sweep (minimal-ats and modern-split) shows micro-compaction firing and collapsing to 1 page, and asserts the invariant that NO page ever strands a single isolated continuation row. (3) RECRUITER DRAWER UI POLISH: the cover letter is no longer a footer glued to the bottom edge of the A4 canvas; it is now a clean tabbed view (Resume / Cover letter) with role=tablist, role=tab, aria-selected, aria-controls, tabIndex roving, ArrowLeft/ArrowRight/Home/End keyboard navigation and visible focus rings, rendering the sanitized cover letter inside its own rounded card container in a separate scroll panel. (4) GUARDS: 100% Linux compatible, zero OS console windows, no winget/cmd/PowerShell, no detached server; src/cv-templates git diff = 0; xampp-policy 4/4. SUPERSEDED CONTRACTS UPDATED: tests/dir066 S4 and tests/dir056 SUB-056-5 previously pinned the removed .html download (buildPrintableDocument x2); they now assert the print path keeps the styled builder and the download is a real PDF/DOCX. EVIDENCE: new tests/dir067-recruiter-export-partitioner-orphan.test.mjs 7/7 (recruiter uses the centralized client with the public endpoints and no URL.createObjectURL; distinct PDF/Word buttons with loading+error states; tabbed cover letter with full aria semantics and the glued footer gone; the public DOCX route is published-only and rate-limited; packSections/COMPACT_SECTION_GAP_PX 11/MINOR_OVERFLOW_PX 60/applyOrphanGuard present; plus the two functional sweeps). Regression: dir064/065/066/067/063 + previews + empty-sections + dir048/055/056 + employer portal 125/125; backend DOCX + parity + export pipeline 38/38; full control surface 2052/2052; product slice 104/104. HEADLESS PLAYWRIGHT EVIDENCE: DOM census over all 55 templates on the gridDense fixture -> CENSUS PASS, no grid card overlaps the page footer (0px on every CV); overflow probe on long (55 templates) -> 0 clipped elements, 0 probe failures. GATES: lint 0 errors (253 pre-existing warnings); security:static 67/67; xampp-policy 4/4; build 'built in 3.14s' (under the 4.0s budget). HONEST LIMITS: the recruiter DOCX export requires the candidate to have PUBLISHED their resume (the same published-only rule as the existing public PDF path), and returns an honest error otherwise - it cannot export an unpublished draft. The DOCX builder has no watermark support, so the public DOCX route gates on the owner entitlement exactly like the existing /api/export-docx rather than stamping a free-plan watermark the way the PDF path does. Mechanism (B) is a safety net: across the swept profile space the row-paired packer already avoids continuation widows, so the guard did not need to fire, but the invariant it guarantees is asserted on every swept profile."
